abstract: >-
  A retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) desktop application for
  scientific literature analysis: it indexes a local collection of PDF
  papers into an embedded LanceDB database using local embedding models
  (Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B, fully offline) or the GWDG Chat AI API,
  retrieves passages by hybrid search (dense vectors fused with BM25
  full-text ranking) refined by a cross-encoder reranker, and reports
  precise source attribution down to file name, page number and the
  individual passages behind each answer. Answers can optionally be
  composed by any OpenAI-compatible large language model; without one,
  the application runs in retrieval-only mode with no API key and no
  network. Includes a desktop graphical user interface and a
  command-line interface, incremental index updates, adjustable
  chunking and retrieval parameters, and export of results.
  Funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG, German Research
  Foundation) under the National Research Data Infrastructure –
  NFDI 38/1 – project number 460247524 (NFDI-MatWerk consortium).
